</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="">
<dc:identifier></dc:identifier>
<dc:title>Effects of cold water immersion after exercise on fatigue recovery and exercise performance--meta analysis</dc:title>
<prism:doi></prism:doi>
<prism:url></prism:url>
<dc:creator><rdf:Bag><rdf:li>Feiyan Xiao</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Anastasiia V. Kabachkova</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Lu Jiao</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Huan Zhao</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Leonid V. Kapilevich</rdf:li>
</rdf:Bag></dc:creator>
<dc:description>Cold water immersion (CWI) is very popular as a method reducing post-exercise muscle stiffness, eliminating fatigue, decreasing exercise-induced muscle damage (EIMD), and recovering sports performance.</dc:description>
<dc:subject><rdf:Bag><rdf:li>delayed-onset muscle soreness</rdf:li><rdf:li>cold water immersion</rdf:li><rdf:li>exercise fatigue</rdf:li><rdf:li>exercise-induced soreness</rdf:li><rdf:li>fatigue recovery measures</rdf:li></rdf:Bag></dc:subject>
